# Next.js Hybrid Rendering

Components default to **Server Components**. Add `'use client'` only at the smallest interactive leaf — never on pages or layouts by default.

## Server vs Client

**Server Component (default)** — use for:
- Data fetching (DB, APIs, `fetch`)
- Secrets and server-only logic
- Static or cacheable UI

**Client Component (`'use client'`)** — use only for:
- State, event handlers, `useEffect`
- Browser APIs (`window`, `localStorage`)
- Client hooks and React context

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — server page, client leaf
// app/products/page.tsx (Server Component)
import { getProducts } from '@/lib/data'
import { ProductFilters } from './product-filters'

export default async function ProductsPage() {
  const products = await getProducts()
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Products</h1>
      <ProductFilters products={products} />
    </main>
  )
}

// product-filters.tsx
'use client'
export function ProductFilters({ products }: { products: Product[] }) {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('')
  // interactive filtering...
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — entire page is client for one button
'use client'
export default function ProductsPage() {
  useEffect(() => { fetch('/api/products').then(...) }, [])
}
```

## Composition Patterns

- **Push the client boundary down** — keep layouts, shells, and static sections as Server Components
- **Pass serializable props** from server → client (no functions, no class instances)
- **Children slot pattern** — Client wrapper renders `{children}`; server passes server-rendered content as children
- **Extract thin client wrappers** for third-party components that need browser APIs

## Streaming & Caching

- Wrap slow/async sections in `<Suspense fallback={...}>` so static shell renders immediately
- Fetch in parallel (`Promise.all`) — avoid sequential waterfalls
- Cache at function or component level with `'use cache'` and `cacheLife()` when data can be reused
- Prefer server fetch + streaming over client-side `useEffect` fetch

## File Placement

| Location | Default |
|----------|---------|
| `app/**/page.tsx`, `layout.tsx` | Server Component |
| `components/ui/*` (static) | Server Component |
| `components/*` (interactive) | Client Component |

Mark server-only modules with `import 'server-only'` to prevent accidental client imports.
